      "caveats": "The abstract does not specify the geographic location, sample size, or the specific cities where the multisource data was collected to train and validate the model.",
      "what": "The study developed a spatial machine learning framework, MGW_LightGBM, combined with SHAP to model residents' green satisfaction using multisource data and deep learning. It analyzed how 2D landscape patterns and 3D green morphologies, such as tree height and canopy volume, nonlinearly influence satisfaction across segregated and informal neighborhoods.",
      "why": "It demonstrates that 3D structural elements of urban vegetation are more influential on resident satisfaction than traditional 2D landscape metrics, while revealing that residents in informal neighborhoods exhibit highly pragmatic and spatially adaptive attitudes toward green space due to economic constraints."
